  "note": "Annual election of one third (five seats), Wednesday 15 January 1913, for the places of William Ballentine, George Ferguson, Robert George Lonsdale, Thomas Livingston (then in Canada) and William White. Nine candidates, three of them retiring members; declared at 10.45 p.m. \"Of the 2,435 voters on the register, 1,774 polled. There were 20 spoiled votes, and 262 illiterates recorded their votes.\" No party labels printed."
